# Pre-mortem marker — fix cli 1.0.4 walker dual-scope
- date: 2026-09-16
- branch: fix/cli-1.0.4-walker-dual-scope-undeclared-hooks
- mode: light (3 luminary lenses, ~30 min per Klein workshop)

## Lens 1 — Linus (adopter contract)
- Risk: dual-write leaks files at ~/.claude/hooks/ that user didn't expect.
  Mitigation: only fires for hook files present in bundle (bundle is the manifest).
- Risk: user has custom ~/.claude/hooks/trace-helper.sh — we overwrite.
  Mitigation: writeSafely uses AlreadyExists refusal; --force needed to overwrite. Default behavior preserves.

## Lens 2 — Feathers (characterization tests)
- Risk: RED test overspecifies — pins impl detail, brittle to refactor.
  Mitigation: assert observable filesystem outcome (files exist at both paths) not walker internals.
- Risk: fixture doesn't include a user-scope hook that sources a helper.
  Mitigation: use session-reflection.sh + trace-helper.sh shape from real dist/lite bundle.

## Lens 3 — Saltzer-Schroeder (complete mediation)
- Risk: dual-write bypasses the scopeMap discipline for security-sensitive files.
  Mitigation: dual-write ONLY for hook files (isHookFile guard); non-hook files unchanged. Scope classification still runs classify() on declared commands.
- Risk: symlink at target path — walker overwrites blindly.
  Mitigation: writeSafely already refuses symlink writes per S-fold; SymlinkRefused path unchanged.

## Risk ledger — top 3
1. adopter overwrite (Linus L1-2) — MEDIUM; mitigated by writeSafely refusal defaults.
2. test brittleness (Feathers L2) — LOW; mitigation is observable-only assertions.
3. symlink refusal on new user-scope target dirs (Saltzer L3-2) — LOW; existing S-fold path covers.

Strongest concern to fold into plan: adopter overwrite. Verify writeSafely refuses AlreadyExists at ~/.claude/hooks/ path before shipping.
